#---------------------------------------------- 1 procedure_scan_while_1 XFAIL
Not a compiler defect -- UNGRADABLE under this harness, not KNOWN-RED. main(args) needs real command-line
argv (the classic Icon options/dash-branch idiom); scrip's OWN driver already supports argv passthrough
(`./scrip file.icn -- args...` correctly populates args, verified live). corpus_suite_harness.py's suite
format carries a stdin sidecar (.in) and a want-rc sidecar (.wantrc) but NO argv sidecar at all, and
run_suite_entry() never threads one through even if the driver could accept it -- confirmed by reading
run_suite_entry/run_all_modes end to end (no argv parameter anywhere in the call chain). Re-reasoned in
place per hq_B's ruling (row icon-master-six-run-graded-reds-cured, 2026-09-03): an .xfail marker asserts
a known compiler bug, and naming a bug that does not exist is a false marker. Adding an argv sidecar is
shared seven-language harness/instrument work (hq_T's lane), not a fleet seat's fixture-level fix -- this
entry stays correctly XFAIL until that lands, but for the reason above, not for a scan/while defect.
#------------------------------------------------- 717 procedure_write_172 XFAIL
SCRIP's real-to-string conversion prints full IEEE-754 double precision (2.0^0.5 -> 1.4142135623730951)
where real Icon rounds to its canonical ~10 significant digits (1.414213562) -- verified live against the
built oracle at /home/resources/icon-master/bin/icon. Narrow real-formatting defect (the runtime's
real->string routine, not the ^ operator itself -- sqrt(2.0) in the sibling witness procedure_write_194
shows the identical truncation gap). Real, undiagnosed-further-than-this defect; not yet filed to a class row.
#------------------------------------------------- 718 procedure_write_194 XFAIL
Same real-to-string precision defect as procedure_write_172 (SCRIP prints full double precision, Icon
rounds to ~10 significant digits): sqrt(4.0)/sqrt(9.0) are unaffected here only because their exact values
are short to print (2.0/3.0), but sqrt(2.0) shows the identical 1.4142135623730951-vs-1.414213562 gap,
verified against the built Icon oracle.
#----------------------------------------------- 719 procedure_every_to_48 XFAIL
Real compiler defect, oracle-confirmed, not a bad ref. `every write(3.0 to 1.0 by -1.0)` -- a real-valued
to-by generator whose results are mathematically whole numbers. icont/iconx v9.5.25a (run fresh this
session) print `3` / `2` / `1`, matching this suite's own `.ref` exactly; SCRIP prints `3.0` / `2.0` /
`1.0` in both modes. Isolated to the to-by generator path specifically: plain `write(3.0)` (no to-by)
already agrees with the oracle in both compilers, so this is not the general real-to-string formatter.
Full detail, isolation, and routing:
FINDING-2026-09-03-seat01-icon-real-toby-generator-prints-trailing-decimal-oracle-does-not.md. Class filed
to hq_B (Icon lane owner); walker scope ends at filing, not a fleet seat's fixture-level fix.
#----------------------------------------------- 720 procedure_every_to_49 XFAIL
Same defect as `procedure_every_to_48` immediately above (ascending direction of the same real-valued
to-by generator: `every write(1.0 to 3.0 by 1.0)`), oracle prints `1`/`2`/`3`, SCRIP prints `1.0`/`2.0`/
`3.0` both modes. See that entry and
FINDING-2026-09-03-seat01-icon-real-toby-generator-prints-trailing-decimal-oracle-does-not.md for full
detail -- not duplicated here.
#------------------------------------------ 727 ladder_rung36_sets_refusal XFAIL
Real compiler defect, oracle-confirmed, not a bad ref. `insert(3, 1)` (first arg not a set/table) --
icont/iconx v9.5.25a (run fresh this session) raises Run-time error 122 "set or table expected" and
aborts after printing only `before` (rc=1); SCRIP prints `before`/`after` and exits rc=0 -- `insert()`
is missing argument-type validation. Isolated to `insert()` specifically: the other 4 rung36 witnesses
(construction, delete+member, union, intersection+difference) all PASS both modes. Not confirmed whether
`delete()`/`member()`/the set-algebra operators share the same gap when given a non-set/table --
untested. See FINDING-2026-09-03-seat01-icon-insert-missing-set-table-type-check.md; owner hq_B (walker
scope ends at filing per MASTER-PLAN.md WHO FIXES WHAT -- did not touch src/).

